{
  "area": "decayfit",
  "doc": "The decay fitters, through the raw registry-driven interface -- decay_fit_setup_vector / DecayFit2 / DecayFitProblem, which exist under those names in all four bindings, rather than Python's setup_vector() and results_as_dict() sugar, which exists in one. These are numerical results, so they carry tolerances; everything else in the suite is exact.",
